---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import prose from "../styles/prose.module.css";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site.ts";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="An independent South African site run by Timothy Brits, with editable messages, sourced explainers and checked aid listings."
  path="/about"
>
  <article class={prose.article}>
    <h1>About {SITE.shortName}</h1>
    <p class={prose.lede}>
      {SITE.name} is for South Africans who want to understand the US blockade of Cuba and act on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      Timothy Brits runs this site as a volunteer in South Africa. It has no staff and no budget, and carries no
      advertising. No party, company or organisation is behind it or endorses it.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>
      You can <a href="/act">write to someone</a> with a message you edit first and send from your own email app or
      WhatsApp. The <a href="/learn">explainers</a> are short, and every claim in them links to its source. The{" "}
      <a href="/give">organisations on the Give page</a> deliver aid, and we check each one before listing it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Donations go straight to the organisation; this site never handles money. It has no accounts, comments or mailing
      list. We do not store the messages you write in the Action Desk. The <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>{" "}
      explains what stays on your device and what the site counts.
    </p>

    <h2>Our position and sources</h2>
    <p>
      This site supports ending the blockade. The explainers include the US government's reasons for keeping it and
      criticism of Cuban policy. We prefer primary sources, such as United Nations records and government documents, and
      label government sources so you can judge their claims. We review articles at least every six months and record
      factual fixes on the <a href="/corrections">corrections page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Reuse</h2>
    <p>
      Written content is licensed{" "}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        CC BY 4.0
      </a>
      : you may share and adapt it if you credit {SITE.name}.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections, suggestions and organisations we should check:{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. Follow{" "}
      <a href={SITE.instagram} rel="noopener noreferrer">
        {SITE.instagramHandle} on Instagram
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
